WEBVTT

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:06.110
You

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.560
Are you alone? If you're not alone, don't mention my name. That's very important.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.880
I don't know. Whom do you want to speak to, please?

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.600
You're obviously not alone. Is it my secretary with you?

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.150
Is she old enough to be sitting up to supper?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.700
Oh, don't ring off, Larry. Please don't ring off.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.360
You can pretend I'm some man, you know. Call me Mr. Johnson.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.380
I know you'll find it quite an effort, but we won't go into that now.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.950
Oh, Mr. Johnson. Well, it's, uh, it's not very convenient just now, Mr. Johnson.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.100
Who's he?

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.640
Oh, he's, um, he's trying to sell me insurance.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.740
Oh, it's very quick of you, Larry.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.220
Make it life insurance, do you mind?

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.060
I'll tell you why that's so funny when I see you.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.490
Well, maybe it isn't.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.220
Maybe it's just a joke in incredibly bad taste.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.080
All right, look, I thought we had this clear.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.770
I'm not interested in any of your propositions,

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.490
and you promise there'll be no more phone calls.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.210
Larry, I must see you.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.640
come over to the house right away without telling anybody where you're going i'm sorry but it's quite

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.370
impossible oh i know you think it's one of those calls where i'm making excuses but i swear to you

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:51.240
this is not one of those times will you come well i'll think about it hello doctor how are you

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:58.120
intrigued miss frobisher intrigued oh really why well i come to the station to pick up my serums

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.290
And what do I find?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:06.520
my neighbor who has a telephone in every room and has walked miles to a phone box in a deserted

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:11.420
station you've been reading too many thrillers doctor actually my line is out of order you

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:16.390
converted me to thrillers miss probisher in any other author's detective stories i spot the murderer

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:21.250
not later than chapter two yours invariably baffle me until the middle of chapter four you have an

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:26.020
unfair advantage you know the way my brain works the dark recesses of the female mind

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.520
I can hardly claim to have penetrated that far

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.900
But I'm a keen

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.070
student of human nature. I like people. Oh, I should be honored to drive you home. I should

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:40.300
be honored to accept. Was it a satisfactory call, Miss Frobisher? Oh, completely, Dr.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:46.480
Henderson. Good, good. So few things turn out the way we expect them to these days. I

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:52.660
get so many wrong numbers on that phone myself. To save your asking, it was a business call.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:59.360
My dear, you don't suppose I was going to pry into your affair. We'd have come round to it.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.520
or later. The dark recesses

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:28.850
of the female mind. Who should let me

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:29.870
drive you right up to the house?

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.630
I don't trust you turning with that steering column.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.010
Besides, a short walk will do me good.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.790
I'll sleep much sounder.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.730
I think one sleeps sounder on one's own, don't you?

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.800
If not sounder, at least more often.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.400
Good night, Dr. Henderson.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:44.870
Good night, Ms. Robeshire.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.270
I'd forgotten you.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.040
Don't I always say goodnight?

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.190
And this is a special goodnight.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.540
Because it's a special night.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.480
I always have a snack for you, don't I?

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.640
Are you beautiful?

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:31.900
Better.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:36.570
What would I do if I couldn't talk to you every night?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.900
Larry will come, Fury.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.760
If you're only human, you could answer.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.860
Maybe I'm not human either.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.600
Nightfall is special.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:08.960
It must be Mrs. Preston.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:11.560
Who are you?

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.560
You are Mrs. Preston, aren't you?

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:16.210
How'd you get in here?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.120
Through the window.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:20.230
What do you want?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:21.740
Your husband.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.400
Tell him George is here, Mrs. Preston.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.030
My name is Janet Frobisher.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.000
Oh, I know.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:29.930
I've seen it on all those...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.920
I've even read some.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.130
You're good.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:35.890
But you're also Mrs. Preston.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:37.640
That's not so good.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.150
I don't know who you are or why you're here.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.770
But if you don't get out at once, I'll call the police.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:49.680
I wouldn't do that.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:55.550
I said not to do that.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.620
The line is out of order anyway.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:00.780
Get your husband.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:02.790
I've already told you.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:03.990
Get him. Tell him George wants him.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:07.990
George who?

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:09.620
Just George.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.500
Well, he's not here. Obviously, nobody's here.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:13.420
Find him.

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:16.350
Well, I think if my husband were here, I'd call for him before now.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.500
All right. We'll wait for him together.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.560
We may have a long wait.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.800
I haven't seen him for months.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:37.420
They're mine.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:44.660
Nice, comfortable fit, size 11.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.100
My, what big feet we have, Grandmother.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.190
What do you want with my husband?

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.270
Look at the front page.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.560
My name is Bates.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:00.730
Bates.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.140
George Bates.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.120
Metropolitan Bank of America.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:07.940
Correct.

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:10.690
You did this?

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:11.780
We did it.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.180
Credit where credit is due, Mrs.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:15.470
We did it.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:16.890
Your husband and I, together.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:19.750
It says here there was a policeman shot.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.190
He shot him.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:29.960
The wounded man was able to identify one of the men as George Bates, an employee of...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.930
the bank. But it was your husband's gun that shot him, Mrs. Preston. It was your husband who pulled

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:55.110
the trigger. But they're looking for you. And I am looking for your husband. When do you expect

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:59.980
him back? I hope he never comes back. He arrived here.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.220
You're early today from London.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.910
Mr. Bates, I don't know what my husband has told you,

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.970
but actually these are the facts.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:09.490
We've been separated for nearly three years.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:12.570
The people around here think he's in Malaya.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.090
I've told them he's a planter,

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:18.290
that I haven't seen him for nearly a year.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:20.840
Is that hat yours, too?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.750
How long have you known my husband?

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:29.870
Since I was transferred from the American branch.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.680
We met and talked. He can talk, you know.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.700
I trusted him. I had a little money. He knew a lot about shares.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.500
And you found out otherwise?

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.640
Yeah. Then we used bank money. That went too.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:45.870
So we decided we'd be smart.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.860
Is robbing a bank smart?

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.820
Well, we bungled it badly.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:53.290
When the policeman showed up, your husband lost his nerve.

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:54.750
He shot him and ran.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:58.780
We'd arranged to meet here. And here I am.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:04.860
Mr. Bates, if I told you you didn't stand a chance of seeing my husband tonight or ever,

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.840
would you go away, leave England?

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:09.160
No.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.470
His papers are here, his passport, everything.

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:14.410
His clothes would fit you.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:15.450
You're about the same height.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:16.330
You may have them.

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:18.070
I'd help you go abroad, give you money.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:18.910
Will you go?

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:20.890
Your husband and I are going together.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.050
He's already fixed passages on a cargo boat.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:23.720
For one.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:24.220
For two.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:25.720
For one, I have the ticket.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.250
I'll give you a thousand pounds.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:32.620
Why not?

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:33.590
The policeman.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.910
If I clear out and he dies, Preston will say I shot him.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:37.140
Well, he may say that anyway.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.900
You have absolutely no proof.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:39.820
Oh, but I have.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:43.780
I've got the gun with his prints on it.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.500
He got me into this and he gets me out.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:51.580
Now, let's not waste any more time.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.860
He came here this morning and you took him in.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:53.280
Where is he?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:11.050
He's in there. The door is locked.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.310
I know. I tried it.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:14.860
Preston!

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.220
Mr. Bates.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:20.300
I'll make it.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:22.660
Nobody can.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:31.400
I killed him.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:33.640
You what?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:37.900
I killed him this morning.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:40.620
Why did you do it?

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:42.320
Because I hated him.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:44.970
Must have been out of your mind.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.100
I scarcely think you're in a position to pass judgment.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:50.900
All right, let's have it.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:52.690
Who is he really?

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.860
At least he was.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:14:59.350
Could have left him.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.280
I did leave him three years ago. I've already told you that.

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:04.230
But what happened then?

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:05.910
Blackmailed me.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:07.610
About what?

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.360
The water people usually blackmailed about.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.260
It wasn't very helpful to my career.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:21.030
Murder make your sales jump? Divorced him.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:23.100
Clever.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.950
He saw to that too. He paid me visit.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.360
What happened this morning?

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:29.980
I really...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.820
Now he came here direct from the bank.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.070
Said he was in trouble and wanted money.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.380
He promised me a divorce if I'd help him.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.040
A thousand pounds and three days shelter.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:41.520
And you agreed?

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:52.270
Give him the money.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.550
He laughed in my face and said,

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:58.210
Now try and get your divorce.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.570
He sat there on the couch and asked me to bring him a drink.

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:07.660
I refused. He became violent and started hitting.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:13.000
I decided that was the last time he'd ever hit me.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:18.260
I brought him his drink and I put something in it.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.750
It was all over very quickly.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.640
So he hit you, did he?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.480
Yes, Mr. Bates.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.170
What made you think you could get away with it?

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.400
It wasn't important at the time.

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:46.270
Well, it's important now.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.180
I was going to wait until night.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:51.230
Yes?

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:56.740
There's a shortcut to the village behind the stables, the tarn road.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:57.590
Tarn?

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.920
It's a natural lake 60 feet deep.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:18.440
Where is it? Have to be. Wait.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:23.540
Stone's from the town side. It's a deserted road, never used.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.320
Who else lives in the house beside you?

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.990
Chris Dale, my secretary. She's away until Monday.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.320
Maids?

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:31.150
A daily.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:33.320
She finished yesterday for the weekend.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:34.900
Who else comes here?

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:36.230
No one.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.180
I've been working on a new book.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:40.660
The only person I've seen for weeks is a Dr. Henderson.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:41.820
Where does he fit in?

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.040
He's the local vet.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:43.920
Drove me home tonight.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:45.930
He's been treating Fury.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:48.300
Did he ever meet your husband?

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:49.480
No one has.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.190
Not even Chris told you they think he's in Malaya.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.400
Where did you get the poison?

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.890
A compound that Henderson made for Fury.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:17:59.790
Hello, boy.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:01.570
What time did Preston get here?

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:03.400
Early this morning.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:04.620
Was he seen?

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:05.640
I think not.

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:06.420
There was a heavy mist.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:07.480
We were alone all day.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.000
The station, the ticket collector.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.720
He was muffled up in a scarf.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:12.760
Taxi?

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:14.370
Walked.

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:15.680
Nobody saw me either.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.100
I traveled on trucks and coal trains.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.100
Nobody saw me, Janet.

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:27.160
No, that's impossible.

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:27.820
Is it? Why?

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:28.820
I won't do it.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:29.920
You'll do as I say.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:31.760
Your husband's dead. You killed him.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:34.240
They can't hang you for it as long as you can produce him alive.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.180
I'll make a good husband, Janet.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.200
Better than he ever did.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:48.030
Someone's coming.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:49.840
Get out.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.620
I'm sorry to trouble you. May I come in?

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:24.480
I hope I'm not disturbing you, Miss Wilbisher.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.700
Well, it is a bit late.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.910
I know, and I should have asked you in the car,

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.250
but you know how vague I am.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.200
I'd like to collect the compound.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:32.800
The compound?

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.440
The medicine I made up for Fury.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.200
Now that he's better, I think it might be safer with me.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:38.850
Oh, you stood up.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:39.900
All of it?

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:40.220
Yes.

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:41.830
And the horse still standing?

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:43.250
Oh, but it's a miracle.

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:45.050
I shall have to put it on the market.

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:47.140
Why?

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:48.060
Is it dangerous?

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:49.700
Well, in large quantities, yes.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.540
I thought I warned you about it at the time.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:52.140
Did you?

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:53.390
Oh, I thought I did.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.450
Well, there's no need to worry.

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:55.990
I wouldn't let anything happen to Fury.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.410
Oh, I'm sure you wouldn't, my dear.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:19:59.980
Only as a favor to me, would you mind?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.680
I'm not telling the chemist about it, you see.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.600
I get all my raw materials from him.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:04.940
And he's very easy-going.

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:11.020
You don't mean to say he's back?

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:11.730
Who?

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:14.120
Well, how stupid of me not to guess.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.730
Now, as your next-door neighbour,

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.010
I think I might be allowed to be the first to receive him officially.

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:20.260
Receive whom?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.140
Well, your husband.

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:25.300
Oh, come now, won't you please introduce me?

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.540
Yes, of course she will.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:34.440
My wife wasn't trying to be inhospitable. Allow me to introduce myself. I'm George Preston.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:38.570
How do you do, my dear sir? Good evening. So you're really Mrs. Preston?

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:40.890
You've been keeping secrets from me.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:46.300
Frobisher's only a pen name. George, dear. This is Dr. Henderson.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:51.250
If I'd have known we were having company, I would have shaved.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:55.660
Oh, nonsense. I'm practically one of the family. I only live on the next door farm.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:58.280
How nice to have medical aid so close at hand.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.600
Oh, don't misunderstand me.

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:04.480
My patients are only animals.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.340
You see, the doctor's a courtesy title.

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:08.480
One might almost say a pen name.

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:10.540
Would you care for a drink?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:11.940
The doctor doesn't drink.

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:14.180
Well, as it's such a very special occasion,

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:15.600
perhaps a little sherry wine.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.080
I only touch alcohol on my birthday.

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:19.970
Janet, dear?

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:25.300
And then I must get back and finish my writing.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.930
Oh, you're a writer, too?

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.130
Oh, nothing cosmic.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.900
A paper for the Royal Society of Animal Medicine.

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:35.580
Which reminds me, my dear, do you think I might borrow your dictionary again for a day or two?

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:36.580
I just think so.

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:37.410
Good, good.

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:39.390
I'm not the only one drinking.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:41.800
We're not exactly in a party movie.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.020
Well, here's wishing you both a long life.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.590
Nothing quite so warming as a...

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:52.880
Anything wrong?

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:55.900
Oh, was I staring?

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:57.700
I'm so sorry, it's a dreadful habit.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.810
Well, to work, to work.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:01.850
I'm very glad, indeed, to have met you, sir.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:04.740
Oh, my dear, the dictionary.

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:06.680
Of course.

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:09.170
Well, the last time, I think you found one in the study.

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:12.010
Shall I get it for you?

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:13.330
No, no, I'll get it.

00:22:14.780 --> 00:22:16.640
You must be jolly glad to be home again, Mr. Preston.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:18.300
Oh, yes, yes.

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:20.040
Malaya, wasn't it?

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:21.180
Most of the time.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:22.800
Is it a hot climate?

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:23.830
Stifling.

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:24.930
Oh, that's odd.

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:26.830
I thought it must be quite temperate.

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:28.480
What gave you that idea?

00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:29.560
Well, your lack of sunburn.

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:34.080
Well, I, uh, I spent several weeks in the hospital up in the hill.

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:37.480
Oh, I'm so sorry. Everything back to normal, I hope.

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:39.290
Fine, fine.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:45.490
A dictionary? Will that do?

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:47.490
Oh, our old friend. Yes, admirable.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:50.180
And now I'm afraid I really must tear myself away.

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:54.380
Duty calls. Thank you for your hospitality.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:55.650
Oh, both of you.

00:22:55.910 --> 00:22:59.520
It really has been a most delightful surprise meeting you.

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:03.220
And welcome back once more to your own fireside.

00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:04.110
Thank you, Doctor.

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:04.760
Goodbye.

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:06.120
Au revoir.

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:12.720
Before all those questions,

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:16.880
you'd have had quite a night's work

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:18.240
pitching two of us into the tarn.

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:20.320
I told you to get out.

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:21.680
Lucky I didn't.

00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:23.780
You seem to be getting into quite a tangle.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:28.400
You've taken his clothes.

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:29.970
I could hardly...

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:34.580
It's wonderful what new clothes do for you mentally.

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:38.690
Too bad this doesn't fit too.

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:43.930
Your husband had good taste in everything.

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:48.520
We're not going through with this.

00:23:48.640 --> 00:23:49.520
You don't have any choice.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:51.140
I'm your husband.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.300
Here, drink this. You're gonna need it.

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:30.250
You

00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:28.750
I know, but Arrogate's from 30 miles.

00:25:29.390 --> 00:25:29.910
That's all right.

00:25:32.270 --> 00:25:33.510
Looks like Janet's asleep.

00:25:33.770 --> 00:25:36.190
She can't be asleep.

00:25:36.550 --> 00:25:38.110
Who is it?

00:25:39.590 --> 00:25:41.530
The secretary and her fiancé.

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:43.060
You said one day.

00:25:43.700 --> 00:25:44.580
He must have gone to bed.

00:26:01.720 --> 00:26:19.350
Who's there? Open up there.

00:26:23.360 --> 00:26:26.120
I'm afraid I can't. The door seems to be jacked.

00:26:31.920 --> 00:26:34.120
Of course, I'm all right. I didn't expect you back till Monday, Chris.

00:26:35.310 --> 00:26:36.350
You remember Larry?

00:26:36.840 --> 00:26:40.670
Quite. My faithful little secretary

00:26:40.670 --> 00:26:43.510
think I might suddenly have a juicy murder to dictate.

00:26:44.110 --> 00:26:46.900
Janet, I do hope we didn't disturb you.

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:50.610
No, I'm only so glad I was still up.

00:26:51.790 --> 00:26:52.910
Just a bit late.

00:26:54.380 --> 00:26:57.060
After all, I'm a bohemian. It's fun for people to drop in.

00:26:57.640 --> 00:26:59.000
Adds to the spice of life.

00:26:59.160 --> 00:26:59.960
I told Larry...

00:27:01.080 --> 00:27:03.330
Oh, so it was his idea.

00:27:03.450 --> 00:27:04.270
I'm afraid it was.

00:27:04.830 --> 00:27:06.530
In the middle of dinner, I turned to Chris and said,

00:27:06.930 --> 00:27:10.290
Do you suppose your employer would mind if we descended upon her for the weekend?

00:27:10.820 --> 00:27:12.240
Chris was doubtful, but I insisted.

00:27:12.670 --> 00:27:13.090
I see.

00:27:13.630 --> 00:27:15.350
I felt a craving for the mountain air.

00:27:17.220 --> 00:27:18.140
Call of the countryside.

00:27:20.100 --> 00:27:21.340
Chris will show you to your room.

00:27:21.480 --> 00:27:22.060
The guest room?

00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:23.680
No, the one at the end of the hall.

00:27:24.300 --> 00:27:25.820
My husband is in the guest room.

00:27:26.610 --> 00:27:26.930
Husband?

00:27:28.300 --> 00:27:28.620
Husband?

00:27:29.320 --> 00:27:29.960
Here's the night air.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:33.660
with unexpected guests. Sounds like Shakespeare, but isn't.

00:27:34.340 --> 00:27:36.100
But I thought that you and he were...

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:40.430
So did I, but it seems that he believes whom God has joined. Very tiresome.

00:27:43.040 --> 00:27:46.000
Well, I feel a little weary. I think I'll go to bed.

00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:52.590
Shall I show you to your room? Oh, Chris, the phone is out of the water.

00:27:53.060 --> 00:27:54.320
Would you have attended to in the morning?

00:27:54.730 --> 00:27:56.250
Yes, certainly, Janet. Good night.

00:27:56.530 --> 00:27:56.810
Good night.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:00.160
Good night.

00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:02.220
Good night.

00:28:37.100 --> 00:28:37.760
What about the hat?

00:28:38.210 --> 00:28:39.150
The tarn with him.

00:28:39.970 --> 00:28:40.830
We should have burnt it.

00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:42.320
We should have a lot of things.

00:28:43.110 --> 00:28:43.650
What about them?

00:28:45.700 --> 00:28:45.960
Good.

00:28:46.630 --> 00:28:47.390
I need a drink.

00:29:18.080 --> 00:29:21.900
As husband and wife, there is a communicating door between our rooms.

00:29:22.060 --> 00:29:22.660
It's locked.

00:29:23.220 --> 00:29:26.160
They say a chair under the handle is even better than a lock.

00:29:26.630 --> 00:29:28.810
A man who knows his place is better than either one.

00:29:37.290 --> 00:29:37.870
Shall we go?

00:31:29.600 --> 00:31:29.840
pressed

00:31:30.090 --> 00:31:30.830
She's out riding.

00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:31.780
Riding?

00:31:32.450 --> 00:31:33.170
Well, what time is it?

00:31:34.220 --> 00:31:34.720
Ten o'clock.

00:31:35.490 --> 00:31:37.910
She said you'd had a very exhausting day and I was to let you sleep.

00:31:40.470 --> 00:31:41.430
You're the secretary?

00:31:43.010 --> 00:31:43.730
Yes, Christelle.

00:31:44.620 --> 00:31:46.800
May I say welcome home, Mr. Preston?

00:31:47.050 --> 00:31:47.430
Thank you.

00:31:47.880 --> 00:31:48.620
When is she coming back?

00:31:49.290 --> 00:31:50.590
Well, that's difficult to say.

00:31:50.830 --> 00:31:52.150
They've been gone about an hour.

00:31:52.580 --> 00:31:52.760
They?

00:31:53.660 --> 00:31:54.800
My fiancé's with her.

00:31:55.560 --> 00:31:55.680
Oh.

00:31:56.890 --> 00:31:58.510
Tell her I want to see her as soon as she comes back.

00:31:59.610 --> 00:31:59.970
Oh.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:05.360
Oh, this is Mr. Piggly. I asked him to call back, but he particularly wanted to wait.

00:32:05.540 --> 00:32:14.380
I can come back if it's inconvenient, but I've cycled up here from the village and I've got a touch of arthritis and...

00:32:15.030 --> 00:32:16.310
What was it you wanted, Mr. Bigley?

00:32:16.560 --> 00:32:22.080
Well, I'm president of the Tarmorotarians Club,

00:32:22.120 --> 00:32:24.340
and we've our annual dinner coming up.

00:32:25.220 --> 00:32:25.880
Very interesting.

00:32:26.680 --> 00:32:29.560
Well, every year we have this dinner because...

00:32:30.188 --> 00:32:31.288
It's annual, you see.

00:32:32.044 --> 00:32:32.604
Obviously.

00:32:33.324 --> 00:32:33.904
Beg your pardon?

00:32:34.924 --> 00:32:37.264
What is it you want, Mr. Bigley? A subscription?

00:32:38.156 --> 00:32:40.956
The Tom or Oterian's Club is not in need of cash.

00:32:41.452 --> 00:32:42.132
And then it's unique.

00:32:42.412 --> 00:32:43.252
And what does it need?

00:32:43.724 --> 00:32:45.584
We were hoping you'd come and address us.

00:32:46.636 --> 00:32:47.296
Address you.

00:32:47.884 --> 00:32:48.324
On what?

00:32:48.556 --> 00:32:50.556
On your experiences abroad.

00:32:51.180 --> 00:32:54.480
Oh, I'm afraid that's not my line, but please thank the club for asking me.

00:32:54.560 --> 00:32:57.220
Last year, young Alf Deeking was demopped from the Navy.

00:32:57.900 --> 00:33:00.000
He gave us a most interesting address on screen.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:00.580
Cup of Flow.

00:33:00.796 --> 00:33:02.456
Well, maybe he can give you another one this year.

00:33:02.592 --> 00:33:03.592
Oh, I don't think so.

00:33:03.804 --> 00:33:05.564
Well, I'm a little out of practice for these things.

00:33:05.684 --> 00:33:06.984
Fifteen minutes, I'm been there.

00:33:07.184 --> 00:33:09.264
Mr. Preston only arrived back yesterday.

00:33:09.484 --> 00:33:09.924
Oh, I know.

00:33:10.492 --> 00:33:11.652
Dr. Henderson rang me.

00:33:12.188 --> 00:33:14.188
That's why we wanted to get in first.

00:33:14.460 --> 00:33:18.040
Well, suppose we leave it open for a couple of days, then Mr. Preston can think it over.

00:33:18.220 --> 00:33:19.600
Yes, yes, I'll think it over.

00:33:20.764 --> 00:33:21.904
Thank you, Mr. Preston.

00:33:22.364 --> 00:33:23.404
You're most generous.

00:33:24.188 --> 00:33:24.888
Good day, miss.

00:33:25.532 --> 00:33:26.152
Good day, sir.

00:33:29.116 --> 00:33:29.416
All.

00:33:30.028 --> 00:33:31.028
I'm gonna show you.

00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:32.460
As president of the club.

00:33:32.716 --> 00:33:34.096
you'll get a most hearty welcome.

00:33:35.020 --> 00:33:35.920
Aye, teachable.

00:33:38.156 --> 00:33:40.596
It just wouldn't do to have scupper floor two years running.

00:33:46.732 --> 00:33:47.952
You're going to get several of those.

00:33:48.300 --> 00:33:48.960
Would you like me to...

00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:49.720
Yes, please.

00:33:50.572 --> 00:33:52.412
News travels fast around here.

00:33:52.588 --> 00:33:55.308
I'm afraid Dr Henderson is the local broadcasting company.

00:33:55.916 --> 00:33:58.276
I'm sorry if I was abrupt just now.

00:33:58.416 --> 00:33:59.356
Oh, that's all right.

00:34:00.156 --> 00:34:02.696
Things must seem rather strange to you after so much time.

00:34:02.836 --> 00:34:03.216
Yes.

00:34:03.516 --> 00:34:04.936
Things are rather strange.

00:34:05.244 --> 00:34:06.684
At any rate, if you need any help.

00:34:06.972 --> 00:34:07.872
I hope you lost me.

00:34:07.996 --> 00:34:08.496
Thank you.

00:34:08.796 --> 00:34:09.836
We'll get along fine.

00:34:10.748 --> 00:34:13.668
We have no daily till tomorrow. Would you like me to make you some coffee?

00:34:13.824 --> 00:34:15.024
Well, that would be very nice of you.

00:34:16.572 --> 00:34:18.192
Oh, I found these in the study.

00:34:18.812 --> 00:34:20.812
Would you like them to be sent to the cleaners?

00:34:21.500 --> 00:34:22.500
Those are...

00:34:22.748 --> 00:34:25.008
Just my gardening clothes, they're hardly worth cleaning.

00:34:27.420 --> 00:34:29.460
Oh, and I'd like my coffee black.

00:34:30.092 --> 00:34:30.972
Right, Ms. Fester.

00:34:39.404 --> 00:34:41.864
more rides like that and I ought to be able to control the horse.

00:34:42.508 --> 00:34:45.328
A few more topics like this and we ought to run out of small talk.

00:34:45.428 --> 00:34:46.068
Have you a cigarette?

00:34:50.316 --> 00:34:50.816
Thank you.

00:34:52.172 --> 00:34:52.452
Janet.

00:34:53.132 --> 00:34:54.492
I love Chris very much.

00:34:54.956 --> 00:34:56.056
I don't intend to hurt her.

00:34:58.060 --> 00:34:59.780
Is that why you brought her with you last night?

00:35:00.220 --> 00:35:00.620
Yes.

00:35:00.780 --> 00:35:01.640
I thought so.

00:35:03.356 --> 00:35:05.796
Janet, why did you send for me last night when you...

00:35:05.948 --> 00:35:07.488
Knew your husband was in the house.

00:35:09.500 --> 00:35:11.260
because I'm a wicked, shallow woman.

00:35:11.804 --> 00:35:13.444
You're about as shallow as that water.

00:35:14.236 --> 00:35:15.456
And that water's pretty deep.

00:35:17.404 --> 00:35:18.744
Why did you really send for me?

00:35:20.860 --> 00:35:22.080
I don't want to talk about it.

00:35:24.252 --> 00:35:25.392
What are your husband's plans?

00:35:26.556 --> 00:35:27.376
He leaves tomorrow.

00:35:27.772 --> 00:35:28.432
Just like that.

00:35:29.052 --> 00:35:29.972
He leaves tomorrow.

00:35:30.572 --> 00:35:32.132
There you were losing a maid.

00:35:32.428 --> 00:35:34.668
Actually, I'd be more upset over losing a maid.

00:35:35.436 --> 00:35:37.516
Unfortunately, we can't lose Chris tomorrow.

00:35:37.696 --> 00:35:39.076
Chris has nothing to do with you and me.

00:35:40.332 --> 00:35:45.452
I should be shocked to find out that my nice little secretary had anything to do with you and me.

00:35:46.764 --> 00:35:48.764
Especially me

00:35:51.052 --> 00:35:51.632
Come on, Fury.

00:35:52.556 --> 00:35:53.776
Let's race him to the house.

00:35:54.124 --> 00:35:55.144
What chance have I got?

00:35:55.424 --> 00:35:57.144
The two of you are practically unbeatable.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:00.080
You

00:36:50.760 --> 00:36:58.920
unbeatable have no comment we'll know something what i don't think you even tried you must give

00:36:58.920 --> 00:36:59.960
me another chance to mock

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:02.520
Well, it's about time.

00:37:02.770 --> 00:37:04.310
Lunch has been ready for half an hour.

00:37:04.720 --> 00:37:05.800
You shouldn't have waited for us.

00:37:05.960 --> 00:37:08.020
Oh, and Mr. Preston wanted to see you as soon as you got back.

00:37:08.430 --> 00:37:09.170
Oh, where is he?

00:37:09.450 --> 00:37:11.110
He's up in his room. He's been there all morning.

00:37:12.180 --> 00:37:13.880
Larry, would you mind seeing to the horse?

00:37:14.310 --> 00:37:14.850
Of course.

00:37:16.870 --> 00:37:17.450
Quick lunch.

00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:24.540
How is the famous Mr. Preston?

00:37:24.770 --> 00:37:25.430
Very strange.

00:37:25.860 --> 00:37:27.900
Doesn't sound like the gayest companion for a weekend.

00:37:28.140 --> 00:37:28.800
No, he doesn't.

00:37:33.580 --> 00:37:34.540
What have you been doing all morning?

00:37:35.650 --> 00:37:39.840
Home typing, while my fiancé goes out riding with the most attractive boss.

00:37:46.080 --> 00:37:46.760
What have you been doing?

00:37:48.640 --> 00:37:49.540
Finding my own business.

00:37:49.820 --> 00:37:52.180
You've got no right to go out and leave me with strange people around.

00:37:53.050 --> 00:37:56.890
Mr. Bates, last night I made you an offer, a thousand pounds and a passport, and you refused.

00:37:57.540 --> 00:37:59.300
Instead, you decided to start a masquerade.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:04.140
Tomorrow the masquerade finishes, and what you do or feel today doesn't concern me in the slightest.

00:38:04.380 --> 00:38:07.620
Mrs. Preston, from now on I'm giving the orders in this house.

00:38:08.010 --> 00:38:08.810
You will leave tomorrow.

00:38:09.050 --> 00:38:11.900
I'm staying indefinite, otherwise I'm telling the whole story.

00:38:12.650 --> 00:38:13.810
It's your word against mine.

00:38:14.110 --> 00:38:14.950
I'll risk that.

00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:23.860
Last night you put a man in the tarn, Mr. Bates.

00:38:24.310 --> 00:38:26.450
The husband is dead. Long live the husband.

00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:29.970
You put a man in the tarn, and he won't...

00:38:33.270 --> 00:38:39.100
Bates only dropped off and you had to hurry, remember?

00:38:39.900 --> 00:38:42.980
Chris and Larry arrived unexpectedly and you had to do it alone.

00:38:46.640 --> 00:38:53.610
A man loaded with weights to 60 foot of water and he wasn't dead.

00:38:55.240 --> 00:38:56.160
You can't make me...

00:38:56.160 --> 00:38:59.330
Do you feel his pulse, Mr. Bates, or his heart?

00:39:00.540 --> 00:39:01.540
You turn on the light.

00:39:02.460 --> 00:39:03.020
You're lying.

00:39:03.440 --> 00:39:03.800
Perhaps.

00:39:08.870 --> 00:39:10.320
You'll never know, will you?

00:39:11.370 --> 00:39:13.360
You'll never be quite sure.

00:39:15.490 --> 00:39:16.230
You're leaving tomorrow.

00:39:18.230 --> 00:39:19.650
Oh, they're waiting lunch for us, George.

00:39:19.810 --> 00:39:20.270
Are you coming?

00:39:23.740 --> 00:39:26.620
Janet! Janet!

00:39:30.730 --> 00:39:33.730
It was a wonderful morning. Fury's never been a spit.

00:39:35.500 --> 00:39:40.160
George, you know Chris, Larry, this is my husband, George.

00:39:40.420 --> 00:39:41.520
How do you do? How do you do?

00:39:41.770 --> 00:39:42.990
How's the work going, Chris?

00:39:43.190 --> 00:39:44.450
Oh, it's coming along fine.

00:39:45.050 --> 00:39:47.230
Did Larry tell you he raced to the house and that he won?

00:39:47.580 --> 00:39:48.280
No, he didn't.

00:39:48.740 --> 00:39:50.440
I always thought Janet was unbeatable.

00:39:50.770 --> 00:39:51.790
And you found out otherwise?

00:39:52.710 --> 00:39:55.730
You know, Fury has never been a spit. It was a glorious morning.

00:40:15.320 --> 00:40:15.820
I'm not going.

00:40:17.020 --> 00:40:17.540
Of this room.

00:40:19.160 --> 00:40:20.380
I'm not a criminal type.

00:40:21.360 --> 00:40:23.100
This thing is too much for me alone.

00:40:24.050 --> 00:40:24.710
You've been drinking.

00:40:25.270 --> 00:40:26.470
Help me think sober.

00:40:27.370 --> 00:40:28.270
And do you know what I thought?

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:41.280
need me as much as i need you we're in this thing together right to the end better or for worse

00:40:42.290 --> 00:40:48.570
in love or in loathing we're married janet can't we discuss this at a more

00:40:48.660 --> 00:40:54.030
reasonable hour there's nothing more to discuss you can go back to sleep

00:41:00.860 --> 00:41:03.120
Oh, from now on, I'll be using this door.

00:41:03.860 --> 00:41:05.260
It'll add a touch of authenticity.

00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:26.580
Fair startle me.

00:41:26.900 --> 00:41:28.570
Good morning. I'm Mr. Preston.

00:41:28.910 --> 00:41:29.870
Mr. Preston?

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:31.020
Yes, I came back Saturday.

00:41:31.490 --> 00:41:33.430
Are you Mrs. Bunting, sir?

00:41:34.180 --> 00:41:36.860
Mrs. Bunting, I come in Mondays to Fridays.

00:41:37.140 --> 00:41:38.860
Oh, yes, I've heard all about you, Mrs. Bunting.

00:41:39.390 --> 00:41:40.330
I've no idea.

00:41:40.590 --> 00:41:41.510
Neither had my wife.

00:41:41.610 --> 00:41:42.790
My return was unexpected.

00:41:43.410 --> 00:41:43.830
Yes, sir.

00:41:44.400 --> 00:41:46.100
Madam must have been very surprised.

00:41:46.440 --> 00:41:47.240
Madam was.

00:41:48.160 --> 00:41:48.900
Do you have any papers?

00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:50.160
Papers, sir.

00:41:50.380 --> 00:41:51.360
Morning papers, newspapers.

00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:52.640
Oh, no, sir.

00:41:53.020 --> 00:41:54.460
Lad usually delivers them,

00:41:54.640 --> 00:41:56.760
but they won't be here for another two hours at least.

00:41:57.230 --> 00:41:57.710
Two hours?

00:41:58.050 --> 00:41:59.770
He has to cycle from Town Moor.

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:03.080
Oh, yes, yes, I've forgotten. It's been a long time.

00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:07.640
Well, I'll probably take one of the horses and ride over for them.

00:42:07.930 --> 00:42:10.630
Yes, sir. Would you be wanting some breakfast first?

00:42:10.930 --> 00:42:11.590
No, thanks.

00:42:11.850 --> 00:42:17.680
Oh, but I'm sure my wife would be most grateful for a cup of coffee.

00:42:18.460 --> 00:42:19.040
Yes, sir.

00:43:37.230 --> 00:43:50.620
If it isn't Mr. Preston, this is an honour.

00:43:51.260 --> 00:43:51.740
A cup of tea?

00:43:51.970 --> 00:43:52.550
No, thanks.

00:43:52.940 --> 00:43:54.780
Whatever brings you into Tarmore at this hour?

00:43:54.940 --> 00:43:55.860
I came for the papers.

00:43:56.680 --> 00:43:57.240
The papers?

00:43:57.930 --> 00:43:59.930
Oh, there's only one and the lad delivers them to you.

00:44:00.410 --> 00:44:01.650
You'll be leaving in a couple of minutes.

00:44:02.190 --> 00:44:03.950
I was rather anxious to see it this morning.

00:44:04.070 --> 00:44:06.360
There should be a review of my wife's new book.

00:44:06.620 --> 00:44:08.000
You don't say. Well, well.

00:44:08.410 --> 00:44:09.750
The new book, what's it called?

00:44:10.170 --> 00:44:12.290
Better read the review first. We may want to hush it up.

00:44:12.860 --> 00:44:14.400
It's not likely. They're all lovely stuff.

00:44:14.780 --> 00:44:15.960
I've got the lot here, you know.

00:44:16.350 --> 00:44:17.530
Is this the only local paper?

00:44:17.690 --> 00:44:18.370
Just the one.

00:44:19.540 --> 00:44:22.180
Did you think any more about our club, Mr. Preston?

00:44:22.320 --> 00:44:22.540
Huh?

00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:25.030
No, no, I'm really not settled in yet.

00:44:25.320 --> 00:44:26.540
Oh, no, of course you're not.

00:44:27.760 --> 00:44:29.540
I like the London papers, too.

00:44:30.030 --> 00:44:32.930
Oh, I'm afraid I can't give you those. They have to be ordered specially.

00:44:33.280 --> 00:44:37.930
We don't get many. A Miss Frobisher, I mean Mrs. Preston, doesn't usually have them.

00:44:38.520 --> 00:44:42.560
Oh, I see. Are you the only paper shop?

00:44:42.740 --> 00:44:45.170
I'm afraid so. I'll tell you what I can do, though.

00:44:45.390 --> 00:44:47.550
I'll ask Dr. Henderson to save you his copies.

00:44:47.980 --> 00:44:49.520
Dr. Henderson gets the London papers?

00:44:49.760 --> 00:44:53.240
Morning and evening. Not for love nor money would he miss those crossword puzzles.

00:44:53.810 --> 00:44:55.050
I'd like to order them tomorrow.

00:44:55.350 --> 00:44:57.450
But, of course, the London papers for Mr. Preston.

00:44:57.670 --> 00:44:59.970
Oh, and I'd rather you didn't bother Dr.

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:02.380
Just as you say, Mr. Preston.

00:45:02.440 --> 00:45:02.740
Yes?

00:45:03.550 --> 00:45:05.250
You won't forget to consider it, will you?

00:45:05.680 --> 00:45:06.240
Consider what?

00:45:07.730 --> 00:45:09.110
The town moralitarians.

00:45:09.370 --> 00:45:10.390
Oh, yes, yes.

00:45:10.770 --> 00:45:14.120
Well, there goes a fine considerate gentleman.

00:45:48.680 --> 00:45:57.970
That thing every day I thought my wife was the writer finish the book the rest is up to me. Am I disturbing you? Oh, go ahead

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:00.540
Anyone up?

00:46:01.630 --> 00:46:03.030
In the middle of the moors by now.

00:46:03.730 --> 00:46:04.090
Riding?

00:46:04.510 --> 00:46:05.030
Of course.

00:46:05.460 --> 00:46:07.140
Fury has to have his exercise.

00:46:07.720 --> 00:46:09.460
He certainly worships that animal.

00:46:09.940 --> 00:46:11.720
Well, he is rather magnificent, don't you think?

00:46:12.110 --> 00:46:13.430
She should have married the horse.

00:46:15.350 --> 00:46:16.310
The break will do her good.

00:46:16.370 --> 00:46:17.530
She's been working very hard.

00:46:19.240 --> 00:46:20.260
When's your great day?

00:46:20.770 --> 00:46:21.150
Larry?

00:46:21.700 --> 00:46:22.980
We haven't decided, definitely.

00:46:23.820 --> 00:46:24.760
Don't wait too long.

00:46:25.950 --> 00:46:26.930
Is that the gypsy's warning?

00:46:27.560 --> 00:46:29.380
It's just a piece of advice for what it's worth.

00:46:30.670 --> 00:46:31.070
Cigarette?

00:46:31.600 --> 00:46:31.880
No.

00:46:32.590 --> 00:46:35.230
I'm one of those awkward people who get ash in the typewriter.

00:46:36.580 --> 00:46:37.240
She go out alone?

00:46:37.910 --> 00:46:39.070
No, Larry went with her.

00:46:39.720 --> 00:46:40.840
She enjoys his company.

00:46:41.740 --> 00:46:42.520
I think so, too.

00:46:43.770 --> 00:46:45.810
Don't you trust your wife, Mr. Preston?

00:46:46.050 --> 00:46:46.670
Not particularly.

00:46:47.150 --> 00:46:49.010
Oh, I can finish this later.

00:46:49.350 --> 00:46:49.890
No, go ahead.

00:46:50.510 --> 00:46:51.410
Where does she usually ride?

00:46:51.820 --> 00:46:52.420
On the moors.

00:46:52.520 --> 00:46:53.420
Which part of the moors?

00:46:53.740 --> 00:46:54.720
Well, that's difficult to say.

00:46:54.820 --> 00:46:55.920
You see, they're pretty big and...

00:47:33.800 --> 00:47:35.100
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:47:37.700 --> 00:47:39.020
Because I'm in love with you.

00:47:39.800 --> 00:47:40.880
I've told you that before.

00:47:42.830 --> 00:47:44.130
Keep this sort of thing in mind.

00:47:44.960 --> 00:47:46.180
I'm clinging to, Larry.

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:47.740
You see, I'm the clinging cut.

00:47:48.480 --> 00:47:52.030
That I don't believe because I know you.

00:47:53.520 --> 00:47:55.520
You're not clinging to me or anyone else.

00:47:57.060 --> 00:47:59.650
Janet, are you in some...

00:48:00.250 --> 00:48:10.250
danger danger are you frightened of something how absurd i've never been frightened in my life

00:48:13.250 --> 00:48:20.370
larry for a man you have disgracefully long eyelashes poor darling your feelings all mixed

00:48:20.370 --> 00:48:27.510
up i want you and i hate you both together

00:48:40.270 --> 00:48:44.760
good morning good morning i was just coming up to see you what did you want to see me about well all

00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:48.810
this time i've been trying to think why your face was so familiar well this morning when i opened

00:48:48.810 --> 00:48:53.950
the papers i found the answer the papers the london papers you obviously haven't seen them

00:48:53.950 --> 00:48:59.970
yet there recognize yourself george bates the bank robber it's been in london

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:04.700
from a snapshot you see you know there is a definite resemblance it's hard to see it staring

00:49:04.700 --> 00:49:09.600
up at you oh don't be too hard on yourself actually it's a purely superficial likeness

00:49:09.650 --> 00:49:16.980
your face is fuller is more healthy i'm relieved to hear it pity about the policeman now what about

00:49:16.980 --> 00:49:21.010
the policeman yes haven't you followed the case the policeman who gave the alarm he's been shot

00:49:21.420 --> 00:49:26.480
he's not likely to recover that means a rope for somebody may i see that paper again please

00:49:26.480 --> 00:49:29.970
certainly old fellow keep it actually it's got the weakest crossword of the

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:35.830
lot well off we go on our respective travels oh I hope I haven't upset you

00:49:35.830 --> 00:49:40.220
with my little joke no of course not good good I knew you had a sense of humor

00:49:40.220 --> 00:49:59.780
they're not back yet I'm afraid not oh mr.

00:50:00.800 --> 00:50:02.800
I've been thinking over what you were telling me.

00:50:03.370 --> 00:50:03.850
About what?

00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:05.860
About waiting to get married.

00:50:06.630 --> 00:50:07.600
Oh, how's that?

00:50:08.800 --> 00:50:10.180
Can we talk about it some other time?

00:50:10.990 --> 00:50:11.810
Yes, of course.

00:50:12.120 --> 00:50:24.310
It's just that I'm that fool Henderson.

00:50:24.800 --> 00:50:25.260
Let him in.

00:50:31.210 --> 00:50:33.810
Ah, the top of a very fine morning to you, my dear.

00:50:33.990 --> 00:50:35.090
Hello, Doctor. Come in.

00:50:35.400 --> 00:50:35.820
Oh, thank you.

00:50:36.730 --> 00:50:38.250
I must be getting feeble-minded.

00:50:38.530 --> 00:50:40.010
I forgot to return you the dictionary.

00:50:40.560 --> 00:50:41.760
Met him on the moors, my dear.

00:50:41.940 --> 00:50:42.760
Just didn't give it him.

00:50:43.220 --> 00:50:43.660
Thank you.

00:50:43.970 --> 00:50:45.410
I'll tell my wife you returned it.

00:50:45.790 --> 00:50:47.050
Now, if you'll excuse me, Doctor.

00:50:47.570 --> 00:50:51.260
Mr. Preston, if I hadn't had to come here this morning,

00:50:51.400 --> 00:50:55.480
I doubt if I'd pluck up enough courage to ask you what I'm going to ask you now.

00:50:55.930 --> 00:50:57.150
Doctor, I don't want to see Marie.

00:50:57.370 --> 00:50:59.970
Oh, won't you humor an inquisitive neighbor by asking him precisely...

00:51:01.300 --> 00:51:02.000
All right.

00:51:03.230 --> 00:51:06.820
You can return a cigarette.

00:51:07.840 --> 00:51:08.920
I don't smoke myself.

00:51:09.450 --> 00:51:10.390
Not a very good brand.

00:51:10.570 --> 00:51:11.970
I'm afraid I carry them for my clients.

00:51:12.670 --> 00:51:13.050
Thank you.

00:51:13.090 --> 00:51:15.510
What do you want to say?

00:51:16.940 --> 00:51:19.750
Mr. Preston, can I help you in any way?

00:51:21.510 --> 00:51:22.330
I don't quite follow.

00:51:22.920 --> 00:51:26.060
Well, for the last couple of days, I've taken the liberty of studying you.

00:51:27.090 --> 00:51:27.630
Studying me?

00:51:27.910 --> 00:51:29.510
Oh, purely for purposes of research.

00:51:29.610 --> 00:51:29.970
You see, I...

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.140
I happen to be a keen amateur psychologist.

00:51:32.730 --> 00:51:34.710
I don't think I like being put under a microscope.

00:51:35.120 --> 00:51:36.280
Oh, I haven't offended you.

00:51:36.520 --> 00:51:38.950
Oh, what have you discovered?

00:51:39.550 --> 00:51:41.010
That you're running away from something.

00:51:43.420 --> 00:51:43.820
What do you mean?

00:51:45.110 --> 00:51:46.150
Oh, not physically, of course.

00:51:46.270 --> 00:51:46.850
I mean mentally.

00:51:47.050 --> 00:51:48.170
You're an escapist.

00:51:50.270 --> 00:51:51.170
What makes you think so?

00:51:51.350 --> 00:51:52.890
Well, your long rides alone,

00:51:53.340 --> 00:51:55.440
your apparent preference for your own company

00:51:55.440 --> 00:51:57.440
to the exclusion of everybody else,

00:51:57.640 --> 00:51:59.140
including your charming wife,

00:51:59.840 --> 00:51:59.980
your...

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.920
running away from something and can't help wondering what it is.

00:52:04.140 --> 00:52:06.320
You study all your friends this way?

00:52:06.780 --> 00:52:09.320
I must say, I find the escapist character fascinating.

00:52:09.860 --> 00:52:13.090
It's an interesting diagnosis, Doctor. I must let you read my diary.

00:52:13.310 --> 00:52:14.950
Oh, I doubt if you keep one, Mr. Preston.

00:52:15.000 --> 00:52:18.500
and you don't look like a man who confides his secret thoughts even to paper.

00:52:18.680 --> 00:52:24.590
What do we owe this honour?

00:52:25.050 --> 00:52:28.140
Good morning. I, uh, I call to return the dictionary.

00:52:28.460 --> 00:52:29.860
My dear, you look great.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.730
Fresh air. It's wonderful on the moors in the early morning.

00:52:32.870 --> 00:52:34.550
So green and washed and bright.

00:52:34.980 --> 00:52:36.540
You should have come with us, George.

00:52:36.820 --> 00:52:39.730
I tried to. But I really must be going.

00:52:39.950 --> 00:52:42.180
I see you're still driving that death trap.

00:52:42.480 --> 00:52:44.940
Yes, but now even I have to admit she's on her last...

00:52:46.340 --> 00:52:46.700
Goodbye.

00:52:46.960 --> 00:52:54.350
Get a good morning, darling.

00:52:54.590 --> 00:52:56.770
Who does he think he is always snooping around here?

00:52:56.970 --> 00:52:58.730
Can't we ever be alone in this house?

00:52:58.980 --> 00:52:59.140
George.

00:53:02.748 --> 00:53:03.588
Be in the study.

00:53:03.588 --> 00:53:05.868
I didn't mean you. It's Henderson. He gets on my nerves.

00:53:09.244 --> 00:53:09.964
I want to see you.

00:53:13.340 --> 00:53:15.080
That is, if Larry will excuse you.

00:53:23.356 --> 00:53:24.356
Marital bliss.

00:53:24.636 --> 00:53:26.056
Not a very good example, is it?

00:53:26.176 --> 00:53:27.716
It's Henderson. He makes him angry.

00:53:27.856 --> 00:53:28.896
Yes, I know. I heard him.

00:53:30.030 --> 00:53:32.330
And while we're on the subject of making people angry,

00:53:32.510 --> 00:53:36.680
why did you sneak in the front door instead of coming in here the quick way?

00:53:36.970 --> 00:53:39.100
Oh, orders. It mustn't stop you working.

00:53:40.390 --> 00:53:41.850
I'm going to ask you a question.

00:53:42.140 --> 00:53:43.060
What is it?

00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:48.450
I don't want to ask you because I know you're going to answer me truthfully,

00:53:48.470 --> 00:53:51.010
and I dread to hear the answer.

00:53:51.210 --> 00:53:52.410
Then ask me just the same.

00:53:56.350 --> 00:53:59.890
Larry, you first met Janet a year ago.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:02.390
when I took you to her birthday party.

00:54:02.490 --> 00:54:02.890
Do you remember?

00:54:03.350 --> 00:54:04.590
Yes, but what's the question?

00:54:06.540 --> 00:54:09.680
Between then and coming here the night before last,

00:54:09.920 --> 00:54:13.130
have you been seeing her without...

00:54:17.680 --> 00:54:19.380
Very well. There you are.

00:54:19.520 --> 00:54:27.700
They're only your fingerprints now, George.

00:54:30.476 --> 00:54:32.476
The party's over.

00:54:32.556 --> 00:54:35.356
They know whom they're looking for, your photographs in all the papers.

00:54:36.396 --> 00:54:38.196
You got away with Henderson, but there'll be others.

00:54:40.076 --> 00:54:42.076
It's time you were moving on, George.

00:54:44.684 --> 00:54:45.564
And if I refuse?

00:54:46.060 --> 00:54:47.140
Oh, you wouldn't be so stupid.

00:54:48.140 --> 00:54:50.380
You may still have the passport and the money.

00:54:51.436 --> 00:54:55.276
It's obvious we don't get along as man and wife and if you leave now, there'll be no questions asked.

00:54:55.628 --> 00:54:55.908
Janet!

00:54:56.268 --> 00:54:56.908
Are you all right?

00:54:57.388 --> 00:54:58.348
There's your boy scout.

00:55:00.480 --> 00:55:03.330
All right, thank you. I just knocked a lamp over.

00:55:04.730 --> 00:55:05.850
Now, why don't we be sensible?

00:55:06.340 --> 00:55:08.940
I've more chance here than on the run, and you've more chance while I'm here.

00:55:09.280 --> 00:55:10.800
I have nothing to run from.

00:55:11.290 --> 00:55:14.090
You're up to your sweet little neck in accessory to murder.

00:55:15.350 --> 00:55:18.390
For the love of heaven, Janet, can't you see it's madness to play against each other?

00:55:19.190 --> 00:55:21.270
Henderson may guess the truth, but he can't prove it.

00:55:21.500 --> 00:55:23.560
Nobody can, as long as we stay together.

00:55:25.370 --> 00:55:27.050
Very well, George, play it your own way.

00:55:27.900 --> 00:55:28.940
Now, if you have no objection.

00:55:30.060 --> 00:55:31.360
I'll join the Boy Scouts.

00:55:51.980 --> 00:55:52.400
Good evening.

00:55:53.388 --> 00:55:54.568
study windows were locked.

00:55:54.924 --> 00:55:55.444
I know.

00:55:55.820 --> 00:55:56.300
I locked.

00:55:57.484 --> 00:55:58.644
You're back early for once.

00:55:59.116 --> 00:55:59.976
Rain's pretty heavy.

00:56:01.050 --> 00:56:01.570
Too bad.

00:56:01.730 --> 00:56:04.470
Where is my dear wife?

00:56:05.450 --> 00:56:07.630
Don't tell me you've tired of each other already.

00:56:07.970 --> 00:56:09.310
She's taking care of Fury.

00:56:10.180 --> 00:56:11.500
We have a rival, Larry.

00:56:12.370 --> 00:56:13.650
She loves that beast.

00:56:14.060 --> 00:56:14.980
I take it you did.

00:56:16.050 --> 00:56:20.170
People who love animals too much seldom love their fellow men enough.

00:56:21.680 --> 00:56:23.560
I do not like the human race.

00:56:23.800 --> 00:56:25.300
I do not like its silly face.

00:56:26.190 --> 00:56:29.980
But give me a puppy for a friend, and I'll be faithful to you.

00:56:30.060 --> 00:56:32.390
Have a drink.

00:56:32.800 --> 00:56:33.740
Not for the moment.

00:56:34.490 --> 00:56:35.470
Go ahead, do you good.

00:56:35.720 --> 00:56:36.740
Help you to see straight.

00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:37.720
No thanks.

00:56:38.380 --> 00:56:39.800
Got it all mapped out, haven't you?

00:56:40.360 --> 00:56:42.380
The engineer knows all the answers.

00:56:43.010 --> 00:56:43.710
Except one.

00:56:44.360 --> 00:56:44.680
Women.

00:56:45.730 --> 00:56:46.890
That's your problem, isn't it?

00:56:48.720 --> 00:56:49.260
Mine too.

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:51.940
Look, don't you think we ought to discuss this?

00:56:51.960 --> 00:56:52.600
Don't worry about Chris.

00:56:52.720 --> 00:56:53.360
She can't hear.

00:56:53.710 --> 00:56:55.030
She's upstairs in her room.

00:56:55.470 --> 00:56:57.030
