Change my jacket.

00:59:28.070 --> 00:59:28.970
Typing's in the study.

00:59:30.120 --> 00:59:31.220
It's finished and checked.

00:59:32.240 --> 00:59:33.500
I put it in an envelope.

00:59:33.960 --> 00:59:34.940
It's addressed to the agent.

00:59:35.620 --> 00:59:36.360
Thank you, Chris.

00:59:46.490 --> 00:59:50.510
Janet, I've got eyes and ears and senses.

00:59:51.100 --> 00:59:52.520
Oh, you've got more than that, Chris.

00:59:53.090 --> 00:59:55.030
But it's obvious you don't know what to do with it.

00:59:56.120 --> 00:59:58.440
You can have any man you want, can't you, Janet?

00:59:59.160 --> 00:59:59.980
Just by snap-

01:00:00.220 --> 01:00:08.310
fingers. You flatter me. I watch you do it four or five times. I'm only interested in one man, Janet.

01:00:09.320 --> 01:00:15.440
Won't you let me keep him? You're learning to use words quite prettily, Chris. I think this job

01:00:15.440 --> 01:00:28.380
has done you a lot of good. Don't take him away from me, Janet. Rather depend on Larry. Does he

01:00:28.380 --> 01:00:29.980
really mean anything to you?

01:00:31.530 --> 01:00:34.080
Do you love Larry?

01:00:38.450 --> 01:00:39.130
I want him.

01:00:40.520 --> 01:00:42.980
I wanted him from the first moment I ever saw him.

01:00:45.440 --> 01:00:46.640
You asked a pretty question.

01:00:47.210 --> 01:00:48.910
I'm giving you the ugly answer.

01:00:51.710 --> 01:00:52.070
Thank you.

01:00:54.510 --> 01:00:56.330
No suicides or anything melodramatic.

01:00:58.240 --> 01:00:59.140
