01:20:39.590 --> 01:20:43.370
Last evening he rushed out without even a hat or a coat before I could stop him.

01:20:43.920 --> 01:20:46.100
Exactly. But he came back.

01:20:48.400 --> 01:20:49.300
Yes, he came back.

01:20:49.580 --> 01:20:51.840
I tell you one thing that'll never come back and that's my jeep.

01:20:52.790 --> 01:20:53.830
It's beyond repair.

01:20:54.730 --> 01:20:55.410
I'm sorry.

01:20:56.110 --> 01:20:57.850
I took a look at it to see if it could be salvaged.

01:21:04.160 --> 01:21:09.160
been down to the water early this morning it was cold and raw but i'm glad i made the effort

01:21:09.160 --> 01:21:27.430
while i was down there i found this man's hat don't you recognize it should i it's your husband

01:21:27.430 --> 01:21:29.910
I saw it at first.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:32.320
Last night he was here, I... it was lying over there.

01:21:33.260 --> 01:21:34.160
I remember it distinctly.

01:21:37.400 --> 01:21:39.010
Yes, of course it's his.

01:21:39.950 --> 01:21:41.690
It must have fallen off in the accident.

01:21:42.090 --> 01:21:44.110
Oh, then he did go out on a hat last night.

01:21:45.670 --> 01:21:46.750
Oh, well, he must have done.

01:21:48.140 --> 01:21:49.620
Oh, Doctor, you will have to forgive me.

01:21:49.720 --> 01:21:51.880
I'm still so... so utterly confused.

01:21:52.920 --> 01:21:55.160
Of course, my dear, it's been a great shock for you,

01:21:55.220 --> 01:21:56.520
and you mustn't distress yourself.

01:21:57.430 --> 01:21:58.490
Well, I must be off.

01:22:02.590 --> 01:22:06.590
I'll take that, if you don't mind. It's a very interesting discovery.

01:22:10.000 --> 01:22:12.740
Who knows what we may find now that they're dragging the tar...

01:22:13.950 --> 01:22:14.670
...the tar...

01:22:30.960 --> 01:22:31.680
What for?

01:22:32.200 --> 01:22:33.440
The insurance company insists.

01:22:33.890 --> 01:22:34.790
Oh, that is ridiculous.

01:22:35.150 --> 01:22:36.530
Well, I'm afraid it's inevitable.

01:22:36.750 --> 01:22:38.830
You see, I found something else down there.

01:22:39.760 --> 01:22:40.660
I couldn't get to it.

01:22:40.700 --> 01:22:42.700
It was lying on some submerged rocks.

01:22:43.060 --> 01:22:46.800
I couldn't even see it properly except to recognize that it was a body.

01:22:47.930 --> 01:22:48.730
The body of a man.

01:22:49.970 --> 01:22:52.860
How he got there and why, it's impossible to say yet.

01:22:53.570 --> 01:22:56.270
There'll be an inquest, of course, and no doubt a post-mortem.

01:22:58.450 --> 01:22:59.810
Oh, if there's anything I can do, my dear.

01:23:00.090 --> 01:23:01.110
You'll telephone me, won't you?

01:23:02.330 --> 01:23:02.810
Au revoir.

01:24:39.630 --> 01:24:40.490
George, I'm frightened.

01:24:40.770 --> 01:24:41.090
Are you?

01:24:41.740 --> 01:24:42.140
Possible.

01:24:42.340 --> 01:24:43.300
I never know about you.

01:24:43.900 --> 01:24:46.140
They'll be up here soon, asking us questions.

01:24:46.590 --> 01:24:47.290
Not us, Janet.

01:24:47.580 --> 01:24:47.840
You.

01:24:57.810 --> 01:24:58.290
I'm leaving.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:01.760
I ought to kill you, but I'm not going to.

01:25:01.860 --> 01:25:03.060
You think I tried to kill you?

01:25:03.240 --> 01:25:04.420
You think that, don't you?

01:25:04.560 --> 01:25:05.420
I don't think it.

01:25:05.520 --> 01:25:06.060
I know it.

01:25:06.400 --> 01:25:08.520
You tried to kill me just like you killed him.

01:25:09.160 --> 01:25:11.020
When I put him in the tarn, he wasn't alive.

01:25:11.220 --> 01:25:11.960
He was dead.

01:25:12.420 --> 01:25:13.540
Completely dead, wasn't he?

01:25:14.510 --> 01:25:16.070
He was dead, wasn't he, Janet?

01:25:16.790 --> 01:25:17.290
Wasn't he?

01:25:19.200 --> 01:25:19.500
Yes.

01:25:21.050 --> 01:25:21.870
Oh, George, don't go.

01:25:22.590 --> 01:25:23.170
Forgive me.

01:25:24.170 --> 01:25:25.070
I lost my head.

01:25:25.150 --> 01:25:25.690
It was fury.

01:25:26.720 --> 01:25:28.020
I was out of my mind with grief.

01:25:28.730 --> 01:25:29.650
Henderson lied to me.

01:25:30.190 --> 01:25:31.590
Made me believe you shot him on purpose.

01:25:33.030 --> 01:25:34.090
Clever man, Henderson.

01:25:34.660 --> 01:25:35.700
George, don't you see what he's doing?

01:25:36.160 --> 01:25:37.460
Trying to set us against each other.

01:25:38.360 --> 01:25:39.200
That means he's not sure.

01:25:39.750 --> 01:25:42.030
We're safe, George, safe, as long as we stay together.

01:25:42.290 --> 01:25:43.250
You've always said so.

01:25:43.390 --> 01:25:44.870
You were right, you've been right all through.

01:25:45.190 --> 01:25:47.910
If you hadn't tried to get rid of me, this would never have happened.

01:25:48.980 --> 01:25:50.100
Poetic justice, isn't it?

01:25:50.140 --> 01:25:51.060
George, take me with you.

01:25:51.220 --> 01:25:52.120
We'll go away together.

01:25:53.040 --> 01:25:54.580
He'll be here soon asking his questions.

01:25:55.530 --> 01:25:56.150
I don't know what to say.

01:25:56.470 --> 01:25:57.650
Something will occur to you.

01:25:57.810 --> 01:25:58.770
It always does.

01:26:00.800 --> 01:26:02.660
No, George. No, George.

01:26:03.390 --> 01:26:04.330
George, stay with me.

01:26:04.980 --> 01:26:05.980
Just for five minutes.

01:26:06.720 --> 01:26:07.320
Talk to me.

01:26:08.070 --> 01:26:08.510
I know.

01:26:08.900 --> 01:26:09.660
We'll have a drink.

01:26:10.020 --> 01:26:10.880
A farewell drink.

01:26:11.310 --> 01:26:12.710
You can't refuse me that.

01:26:14.420 --> 01:26:16.100
Yes, there is a way out even now.

01:26:16.990 --> 01:26:17.970
Clear cut and plausible.

01:26:18.210 --> 01:26:18.490
What?

01:26:19.280 --> 01:26:19.680
Suicide.

01:26:20.320 --> 01:26:21.180
Not yours, mine.

01:26:22.270 --> 01:26:23.210
I killed your husband.

01:26:23.500 --> 01:26:25.180
Forced you to accept me in his place.

01:26:25.440 --> 01:26:26.960
I threatened you, frightened you into it.

01:26:27.670 --> 01:26:29.970
When I saw them dragging the tarn, I knew it was all over and I...

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:36.420
took my own life. Yes, that would let you out. But first you'd have to kill me. Oh, George, you're mad.

01:26:37.570 --> 01:26:45.440
Now let's think how you'd set about it. Same means as before. Persuade me to take a drink and put

01:26:45.440 --> 01:26:50.760
something in it. I swear to you there's nothing in this drink. I swear to you. Yes, Janet, I'll have

01:26:50.760 --> 01:26:54.600
a farewell drink with you. Out of a flask I filled myself.

01:27:04.600 --> 01:27:18.860
all right if that's the way you want it what's so funny life i'm glad you can laugh here's to

01:27:18.860 --> 01:27:29.850
a long one oh by the way henderson was right about fury

01:27:30.660 --> 01:27:37.370
Strange to see this happening again.

01:27:38.210 --> 01:27:42.560
It takes less than a minute, George.

01:27:44.090 --> 01:27:45.970
And the joke is you did it to yourself.

01:27:52.160 --> 01:27:57.460
Janet, get Henderson, you know.

01:28:07.230 --> 01:28:09.630
Thank you for the way out, George. It hadn't occurred to me.

01:28:10.860 --> 01:28:13.820
You're right, it's a good one. I think it will work.

01:28:16.190 --> 01:28:22.340
Till death do us part, just as you said. Do you hear me?

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:31.060
No, you don't hear me.

01:28:51.980 --> 01:28:52.940
I was just phoning you.

01:28:53.700 --> 01:28:57.080
I came to the room and I found him lying here.

01:28:59.300 --> 01:28:59.900
It's suicide.

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:13.000
I think he's not my husband I know I've known all along I met your husband the day he arrived

01:29:13.000 --> 01:29:27.610
the mist brought him to my door first I directed him here I think I'm going drink this

01:29:36.220 --> 01:29:44.740
I've never done that before.

01:30:00.800 --> 01:30:01.540
Ha, ha, ha, ha.
